    {
      "severity": "info",
      "code": "EML155",
      "message": "\"SUPPLIER_INVOICE_LINE\" is a line item of \"SUPPLIER_INVOICE\", which is itself a line item of \"SUPPLIER\", so \"SUPPLIER_INVOICE_LINE\" is generated as a top-level entity.",
      "line": 2445,
      "hint": "A line item's tab sits one level inside a top-level entity's window; there is no third level. \"SUPPLIER_INVOICE_LINE\" keeps its foreign key supplier_invoice_line_id but gets a window and a dashboard card of its own, and the SUPPLIER_INVOICE page does not list it. If that is what you want, remove the `parent:` directive and the note goes; to list it under \"SUPPLIER\" instead, give it a foreign key to \"SUPPLIER\" and declare `parent: SUPPLIER`.",
      "autoFixable": false
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "code": "EML149",
      "message": "\"MEDICATION_ADMINISTRATION\" looks like a line item of \"MEDICATION\" but declares no parent.",
      "line": 648,
      "hint": "If a list of every MEDICATION_ADMINISTRATION away from its MEDICATION is not a screen anyone opens, declare `%%entity MEDICATION_ADMINISTRATION parent: MEDICATION` — the dictionary then drops its dashboard card and gives it a tab inside the MEDICATION window, linked on medication_administration_id. If it is a thing in its own right, leave it: a reference is the opposite on all three questions (§3.5.1).",
      "autoFixable": false
    },
    {
